<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 1 – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 20px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 9th Grade (CEFR: A2.4)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Ocean Life and Conservation</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Plants That Live in the Ocean</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Analyze the tone and purpose of spoken advertisements. Interactive: Participate in group problem-solving sessions.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can analyze the tone and purpose in Public Service Announcements (PSAs) from local organizations about marine conservation (e.g., "Identify if a PSA about the Panama Bay wetlands by MarViva is persuasive or informative." "Determine if a government announcement about protecting mangroves is raising awareness or promoting action.")<br>Can ask questions to clarify information on marine life (e.g., "Why is it important to protect coral reefs from pollution?" "Reefs provide a habitat for a lot of ocean life.")<br>Can participate in group problem-solving discussions by sharing actionable ideas to protect Panama's oceans and coastal ecosystems (e.g., "Suggest organizing a mangrove replanting day in Juan Diz to reduce erosion and protect marine life." "Propose creating an educational campaign in schools to teach students about avoiding single-use plastics." "Recommend participating in a beach cleanup at Isla Taboga to reduce plastic waste and raise awareness about marine conservation.")</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 35%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 45%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of images showing different plants that live in the ocean, such as seaweed, mangroves, and coral reefs. Students observe the pictures. The teacher asks, "What do you see in these pictures?" and "Where do these plants live?" to activate prior knowledge about the theme "Plants That Live in the Ocean."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces key vocabulary words related to the theme, such as "seaweed," "mangroves," "coral reefs," "ecosystem," "habitat," and "protect." The teacher models the pronunciation of these words, focusing on stress in multisyllabic words (e.g., "ecoSYStem," "proTECT") and minimal pairs (e.g., /iː/ in "reef" vs. /ɪ/ in "riff"). The teacher uses gestures and points to the images for meaning clarification.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of the new vocabulary.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is 'seaweed' an animal or a plant?" (Expected answer: A plant.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is a 'habitat'?" (Expected answer: A place where animals or plants live.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If something is 'endangered', is it safe or in danger?" (Expected answer: In danger.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Ocean Life and Conservation."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short (approx. 90-second) Public Service Announcement (PSA) audio clip from a local organization (e.g., MarViva or ANAM) about the importance of mangroves or coral reefs in Panama. The PSA will contain target vocabulary (e.g., "mangroves," "coral reefs," "habitat," "protect," "ecosystem," "species," "pollution") and present simple/modals.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will listen for the main idea and specific details to understand the tone and purpose of the PSA.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question (First Listening):</b> "What is the main topic of this advertisement? Is it about ocean animals or ocean plants?" (Focus on 'Plants That Live in the Ocean').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (Second Listening):</b> Students listen again and decide if the following statements are True or False based on the audio:
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Mangroves protect the shoreline from waves." (True)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Coral reefs are a habitat for many species of fish." (True)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Pollution does not affect marine plants." (False)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Listening for specific vocabulary (mangroves, coral reefs, habitat, ecosystem, protect, pollution, species) and grammar structures (Present Simple for facts, Modals for suggestions and obligations).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Cloze Activity):</b> The teacher distributes a handout with short sentences or phrases taken from the PSA, but with key vocabulary words (e.g., "mangroves," "ecosystem," "protect," "pollution") missing. Students listen to the PSA again and fill in the blanks.
                        <br>Example: "We _________ our oceans to keep marine life safe." (protect)
                        <br>"__________ provide a home for many fish species." (Mangroves)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled (Sentence Categorization):</b> The teacher plays short individual sentences from the PSA. After each sentence, students (individually or in pairs) identify its tone and purpose: "Is this sentence raising awareness, describing a problem, or proposing an action?"
                        <br>Example: Teacher plays, "Pollution is destroying our coral reefs." Students identify: "Describing a problem."
                        <br>Teacher plays, "We should plant more mangroves." Students identify: "Proposing an action."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction (Listen & Discuss):</b> Students work in pairs. The teacher plays short prompts related to marine life and conservation. One student listens and states the main idea or purpose, then the other student asks a clarifying question or adds a related suggestion using target vocabulary and modals.
                        <br>Example: Teacher plays: "Coral reefs are home to many species."
                        <br>Student A: "The audio says coral reefs are important habitats."
                        <br>Student B: "Why is it important to protect coral reefs from pollution?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Ocean Life and Conservation."</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Problem-Solving Discussion (Mini-Debate/Suggestion Session).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups of 3-4. The teacher plays a short (30-second) audio clip describing a specific problem related to ocean plants in Panama (e.g., "Plastic waste is affecting mangrove ecosystems in Juan Diaz," or "Overfishing near Isla Taboga is damaging seaweed beds which fish depend on for food and habitat").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After listening, each group must:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. Identify the specific problem mentioned in the audio clip.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. Discuss and propose at least two actionable ideas to solve or mitigate the problem, using modals for suggestions (e.g., "We should organize a beach cleanup," "We could create an educational campaign"). They must use at least three target vocabulary words (e.g., "pollution," "mangroves," "protect," "habitat," "conservation").</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency in discussing, collaborative interaction, applying listening comprehension to identify problems, and using appropriate vocabulary and grammar to propose solutions. The emphasis is on sharing actionable ideas as per the learning outcome.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on students' ability to analyze the purpose of spoken input and participate in problem-solving discussions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group briefly presents one problem and one solution from their discussion in Stage 4. The teacher plays a final short audio statement (e.g., "Protecting our coastal areas is vital for biodiversity.") and asks students to identify if it is raising awareness or promoting action. Students then orally state the purpose and their proposed action.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of key vocabulary (e.g., "ecosystem," "biodiversity," "conservation").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accurate identification of the tone and purpose of spoken inputs.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of modals for suggestions and obligations (e.g., "We should protect...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and relevance of proposed conservation actions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Active and collaborative participation in group discussions.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions on a small slip of paper:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new words about ocean plants did I learn today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Could I understand the main idea and purpose of the audio clips?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was challenging about listening to the PSAs and discussions today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can listening to information about ocean conservation help us protect our environment?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson? (e.g., student engagement with audio clips, group participation).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students struggling with listening comprehension or active participation? (e.g., providing visual cues during listening, pre-teaching more vocabulary).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Were the pronunciation points addressed effectively?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Lesson 2: Reading Comprehension), students will read an informative text that uses the same vocabulary and concepts about "Plants That Live in the Ocean" to deepen their understanding of marine ecosystems and conservation efforts.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>